flowchart TB
    accTitle: The reply to a discussion
    accDescr: Someone other than Dennis or a bot opens a discussion or comments on one. A discussion of Dennis, and one whose answer was chosen, end there. Otherwise the pager shows it in its topic and asks the control repository for a draft at once, which Claude writes in Dennis's voice. The draft comes with Send, Edit and Ignore. Send posts exactly that draft as the pager's app, in the thread of the comment that it answers, or on the discussion itself. A new comment of someone else makes itself the message to answer, with a new draft, in the same topic, while a text that Dennis wrote himself stays the draft. When Dennis replies on GitHub itself, an answer is marked, or the discussion is closed, the thing is done: its buttons go, and its topic gets a check mark.

    asked["`**💬** Someone else opens a discussion or comments on one`"]
    quiet["`A discussion of Dennis, or one with its answer chosen: nothing happens`"]
    shown["The pager shows it in its topic and asks the control repository for a draft"]
    draft["`**✍️** Claude drafts a reply in Dennis's voice: ✅ Send, ✏️ Edit, ✖ Ignore`"]
    press["Dennis presses ✅ Send, or edits the draft first: his own text stays the draft"]
    reply["`**✅** The app posts exactly that draft, in the thread of the comment that it answers`"]
    ended["`**✅** Dennis replies on GitHub, an answer is marked, or the discussion closes: the thing is done, without buttons`"]

    asked -- "Dennis's, or answered" --> quiet
    asked -- "anyone else's" --> shown --> draft --> press --> reply
    reply -- "a new comment of someone else: a new draft, in the same topic" --> shown
    draft -- "dealt with on GitHub" --> ended

    classDef you fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class asked,press you
    class quiet,shown,draft bot
    class reply,ended done
